# CX hotkeys -- armed keys.  Copy to  ~/.config/cx-hotkeys.cfg
#
# One SDL keycode (SDLK) per line. These are the keys you consent to have sent to
# the server when pressed. The server decides what each key does (the client does
# not map keys to actions -- it only "arms" them).
#
# SDLK is what the client's key handler actually delivers -- NOT Windows VK codes.
# The two differ: letters are lowercase ASCII (f = 102, not 70), and function keys
# live in SDL's 0x40000000 range. Digits happen to be identical in both, which is
# why bare-number keys "just worked" before this was pinned down.
#
# This file IS your consent: ONLY keys listed here are ever observed or sent.
# Presses are rate-limited to one every 250 ms, and never sent while the game is
# unfocused or you are typing in chat / a NUI text field.
#
# Common SDLK codes:
#     a..z = 97..122   (e.g. f = 102)      0..9 = 48..57
#     F1 = 1073741882 ... F12 = 1073741893 (F1 + n-1)
#     Space = 32   Return = 13   Tab = 9   Backquote(`) = 96
#   Full list: SDL_keycode.h (SDLK_*), or ./sym.sh has nothing -- these are SDL's.

102             # f
1073741882      # F1
1073741883      # F2
